'''Diamond Matter'''{{Refn|[[:File:Mutant (2438).png]]|name = subtitles|group = credits}}<ref name="Mutant Ray"/> is the [[Combinations (Classic)|combination]] of [[Diamondhead (Classic)|Diamondhead]] and [[Grey Matter (Classic)|Grey Matter]]'s DNA. He cannot be accessed unless the faceplate of the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] is broken or by using the [[Biomnitrix]].{{Refn|group = note|name = fusions|Diamond Matter, [[Heat Jaws]], and [[Stink Arms]] are three fusions which were originally created by a broken, [[Omnitrix (Original)|prototype Omnitrix]]. All three fusions are possible with the [[Biomnitrix]]. However, they might differ in aspects such as appearance, powers and weaknesses as there is no evidence that the broken prototype Omnitrix creates fusions the same way as the Biomnitrix.}}

==Appearance==
Diamond Matter is slightly bigger than [[Grey Matter (Classic)|Grey Matter]]. He has [[Diamondhead (Classic)|Diamondhead]]'s crystalline skin, as well as the spikes on his back and head, and Grey Matter's eyes and mouth.

Diamond Matter wears a uniform that is white with black cuffs on the left and black with white cuffs on the right, and wore the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] symbol on his chest.

==Powers and Abilities==
<gallery type="slideshow">
Mutant (955).png|Shapeshifting
Mutant (1056).png|Enhanced Durability
Mutant (1156).png|Weapon Manifestation (via Shapeshifting)
</gallery>
Being part-[[Petrosapien (Classic)|Petrosapien]], Diamond Matter can alter the shape of his limbs like [[Diamondhead (Classic)|Diamondhead]].

Being part-[[Galvan (Classic)|Galvan]], Diamond Matter has enhanced intelligence.

Diamond Matter has enhanced durability, as he was able to withstand being slammed into a branch by [[Heatbat]].

==Weaknesses==
[[File:Mutant (943).png|thumb|218x218px|Small Size]]
Diamond Matter's enhanced strength is reduced due to his size.

Like [[Grey Matter (Classic)|Grey Matter]], Diamond Matter's small size makes him unsuitable for physical battle.

==History==
===Ben 10===
*Diamond Matter first appeared in ''[[Dr. Animo and the Mutant Ray]]'', where he battled [[Heatbat]] and briefly got eaten, then thrown up by an alligator. He then sliced his way through some swamp trees to clear the [[Team Tennyson (Classic)|gang's]] airboat's path until he reverted.

